-- title:
--   Smoothness of the full-level integral model on the Igusa branch
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'\ge 1$ a natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb Q$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K\subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$ be the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $q^2M'$ and group $H=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(X)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise images of that rational function field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with perfect residue field, such that $q$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$, $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, and $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of the quotients $x/y$ of power series over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_A$. Write $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) $A$ $K$ $j$, the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the rings of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively over $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $z\in\mathfrak X$ be a point at which the image $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$, taken through the structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ on global sections and then the germ at $z$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk. Assume: for every prime $y$ of either chart algebra whose image under the canonical morphism to $\mathfrak X$ is $z$, every element $b$ of that chart algebra which is a non-unit of $W_0$ lies in $y$; and for every prime $y$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra over $z$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from that chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, one has $\varphi(j)\notin$ [`ModularCurve.ssJSet`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) $q$ $\Omega$, the set of those $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Then there is an open subscheme $U\subseteq\mathfrak X$ with $z\in U$ such that the open immersion $U\to\mathfrak X$ followed by `toBase` is a smooth morphism.
--
--   This is the smoothness statement for the two-chart integral model over $A$ of the modular curve of level $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ at those points of the special fibre lying on the $\infty$-Igusa branch (the centre of the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$) and not above a supersingular $j$-invariant, cusps included. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_opens_smooth_comp_toBase_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_opens_smooth_comp_toBase_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel), which repackages the conclusion in terms of the project's notion of a good point.
